WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.490
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.470
A few years ago, our next guest signed a

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.629
record-setting podcast deal
worth 60 million dollars.

00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:11.069
(audience cheers)

00:00:11.069 --> 00:00:11.940
What?

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.460
Now with over 5 million
listeners each week,

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.760
her show has been the second
most popular podcast on Spotify

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.144
for the last two years. (horn noise)

00:00:20.144 --> 00:00:22.530
The show is Call Her Daddy.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.260
It's a feminist forward
celebrity interview show where

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.470
guests often feel safe enough
to be vulnerable and honest

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.303
which is cool.

00:00:29.303 --> 00:00:32.430
New episodes premiere Wednesdays
exclusively on Spotify.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.229
Everybody say hello to Alex Cooper.

00:00:34.229 --> 00:00:37.679
(audience cheers)

00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:40.512
(energetic music)

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:51.892
(audience cheers)

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.903
They're going nuts for you!

00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:01.419
- They're Daddy Gang!

00:01:01.419 --> 00:01:03.840
(audience cheers)

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.840
- Congratulations on all
the success of the podcast.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.368
Did you see that happening?

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.023
- You know, I hoped for it.
- Yeah dreamed it, yeah.

00:01:10.023 --> 00:01:12.660
- When you start something
you're like, "I hope"

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.890
But also I was at one point

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.810
like doing it in my parent's basement.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.820
Like, you're like, "I hope this tracks."

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.770
And then the success truly feels

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.270
like still to this day
I'm like, "Pinch me."

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.103
I'm like, where am I?

00:01:22.103 --> 00:01:23.100
I'm on "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.690
Like I'm the biggest
fan, just so you know.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.523
- Oh my God, thank you!

00:01:25.523 --> 00:01:27.840
- My first ever concert was you.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:28.673
- Don't.

00:01:28.673 --> 00:01:29.820
(audience cheers)
- Atlantic City, yeah, yeah.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:30.970
- Are you serious?

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:34.380
- First ever show, my best
friend from childhood, Kristen,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.780
my sister, and my mom,
we went to Atlantic City.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.912
Breakaway.

00:01:37.912 --> 00:01:41.040
- I remember that tour, yeah.
- Oh, I was like thriving.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.450
I think I peaked in that moment.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.380
But yes, I'm a huge fan.
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.210
I love you. I love you. Bow down bow down.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.043
- [Kelly] Oh my God.
- Love you.

00:01:46.043 --> 00:01:47.430
- Well, I have to ask- Thank you.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.230
But I have to ask you,
where did you come up with

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.310
Call Her Daddy?

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.780
- Okay. So I know it's such-

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.740
- 'Cause it seems kind of funny.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.417
- Yes, everyone, especially
my grandmother used to be like

00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:56.520
"What is the show name?"

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.500
I'm like, "Grandma, just listen."

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.520
And I know.
- Yeah

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.880
- So Call Her Daddy was
really, I think the connotation

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.540
of the word "Daddy" in America
is like a man that's a boss

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.940
and powerful and rich and
successful and a leader.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.610
And I was like, let's
flip the gender roles.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.840
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- I'm the daddy too.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.670
And so we changed it to Call Her Daddy.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.410
- [Kelly] I like it!
(audience cheers)

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.000
I love it actually.
- Yeah.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.910
- So you, you signed reportedly
the biggest podcast deal

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.403
in history for a woman.

00:02:23.403 --> 00:02:25.380
That's insane.
(audience cheers)

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.477
I'm gonna lead with that.

00:02:26.477 --> 00:02:28.140
It's 60 million dollars.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.120
So like what, what was
your path to getting

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.080
to that kind of success?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:31.957
Because other people are like,

00:02:31.957 --> 00:02:33.672
"I'm gonna start a podcast tomorrow."

00:02:33.672 --> 00:02:35.512
- Yeah. It's a lot of work.

00:02:35.512 --> 00:02:37.327
I'm not gonna sugarcoat it and be like,

00:02:37.327 --> 00:02:38.580
"Ah, easy peasy."

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.600
- [ Kelly] Yeah.
- It was a lot of work

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.632
but I will say it was the
most rewarding thing because

00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:44.610
I've always been so passionate

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.490
about creating content
and so I was fortunate

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.130
that I was kind of able to take my passion

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.520
and turn it into my purpose and do this.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.400
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- But I will say throughout-

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.390
- That's a gift, not everybody has that.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.770
- Thank you, thank you.
- Yeah.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.710
- I will say though,
something I think that's very

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.830
very unique about my
situation is my relationship

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:02.880
to my audience.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.920
The Daddy Gang who's in
the stands, love you.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.660
- [Kelly] Yeah.
(audience cheers)

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.210
- But truly like I,
everything I do for the show

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.920
has always been for them.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.960
And we have this like
very deep connection.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.947
Like when I'm on the
street, my mom will be like,

00:03:14.947 --> 00:03:16.740
"Oh my God is that a
friend from high school?"

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.200
I'm like, "No Mom, that's Daddy
Gang we met 15 seconds ago.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.210
She's telling me about her
breakup with her boyfriend

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.199
because of the show", like,
we just have this bond,

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:24.690
- [ Kelly] Yeah!
- And I think it's because

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.190
of how intimate the
show is, so I think the-

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.240
- You're conversational.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.970
- Yes, and I think that's why
it's been successful is like

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.763
it's like a family and it
doesn't feel like a show.

00:03:32.763 --> 00:03:34.860
- Yeah. Oh my gosh, I love it.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.814
So more recently you did a docu-podcast.

00:03:36.814 --> 00:03:38.670
This is super cool, about women's rights

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:39.782
titled "An Abortion Story".

00:03:39.782 --> 00:03:42.720
Can you tell us about that
and why you wanted to make it,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.010
why you felt it was important?

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:48.030
- So I think we all see
people online, you know

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.250
influencers who I think
are trying to do a good job

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.680
but sometimes people are
just reposting things when

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.540
something in the news is
happening and they're trying to

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.550
support, but it's like,
did you do the research?

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.960
Like do you know what that means?

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.120
Do you know actually what's behind that?

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.040
Do you know the organization?

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.410
So when Roe v. Wade was
overturned, I just felt

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.900
like I have the biggest female podcast.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.130
There was a bit of-
- And you're female.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.180
- Yes. Yes.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.490
So there was a responsibility
that I felt personally

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:15.180
connected to of, I'm not here
to tell anyone what to believe

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.460
and what to do, but I,
what I wanted to do was to

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.340
create a piece of content that
would be thought-provoking

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.130
and just have people think
about what's going on

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:23.963
in the world.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:24.796
How do you feel about it?

00:04:24.796 --> 00:04:25.860
I didn't ask for anything.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.584
And so I went and I flew to
North Carolina and I went

00:04:28.584 --> 00:04:31.014
to a health clinic that
was giving women abortions

00:04:31.014 --> 00:04:33.690
in North Carolina just to
understand what was going on.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.580
And it took me a few months to do this.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.443
I wanted to make sure I did the research.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.020
I wasn't putting out false information.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.850
I wanted to be as unbiased as I could be.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:42.683
And just be there.

00:04:42.683 --> 00:04:44.070
- Because it sucks because
there is so much news out there

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.000
and you don't know who to trust.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:45.833
- [Alex] Yes, yes.
- Yeah.

00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:48.180
- And I recognize people
come to Call Her Daddy

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.700
to just have a good time and to connect.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.100
And this was the first
project that I ever did,

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.160
truly that was

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.230
way more intense and very serious

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.547
and a little bit more on the side of like,

00:05:00.547 --> 00:05:03.030
"Oh, Alex like you're getting
into certain territory."

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.250
And I'm like, as women,
I think we should just

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.540
have the conversation.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.650
Let's just talk about it.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.577
Let's, let's not-
(audience clapping)

00:05:08.577 --> 00:05:10.320
- Not forcing an answer but like-

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.317
- Yeah! Yeah that's all.

00:05:11.317 --> 00:05:14.070
- I like that, that's what I,
people always say to, you know

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.810
steer away from, from politics or faith.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.797
But I enjoy those conversations most times

00:05:17.797 --> 00:05:19.706
because I like learning.

00:05:19.706 --> 00:05:23.005
I like knowing why you feel so
adamant one way or the other.

00:05:23.005 --> 00:05:25.770
I think, I think that's how
you learn and we progress

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.110
- And I think you just
have to learn to respect.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.510
Like we all clearly have an idea

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:31.920
of why we believe something.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.070
You have to respect both
sides to try to come

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:35.940
to common ground.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:36.810
And that's what I tried to do.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.760
I'm like, I'm not gonna put a PSA of like

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:39.660
this is what you need to do.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.950
Like, just watch it.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.350
And then if you're still-
if you believe one thing

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.310
or another, great.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.590
It's just at least you know,
you made an educated decision

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.423
on how you feel.

00:05:47.423 --> 00:05:49.080
Not just based off of what
your parents taught you

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.580
or what you saw online.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.493
Like how do you feel about the situation?

00:05:52.493 --> 00:05:53.910
Make an educated decision.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:54.743
- Educate yourself. Yeah.

00:05:54.743 --> 00:05:55.980
Yeah. Well we need another break.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.440
You can listen to Alex's podcast

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.210
Call Her Daddy exclusively on Spotify.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.013
New episodes premiere Wednesdays.

